  ROOT CAUSE ANALYSIS:
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  v36 ACK (ci260410182936): SAX parse exception at line 71:
    cvc-complex-type.2.4.a: Invalid content was found starting with
    element '{"urn:hl7-org:v3":author}'.
    One of '{reference, component, outboundRelationship, subjectOf1,
    subjectOf2}' is expected.

  FINDING: The CDER PORR schema does NOT allow <author> as a direct
  child of <investigationEvent>. The valid content model after the
  header (id, code, effectiveTime, availabilityTime) requires the
  reporter block to be wrapped in subjectOf1/controlActEvent/author.

  This invalidates the v35/v36 approach (inspired by JC5H reference).
  JC5H likely uses a different schema or pathway; it is NOT applicable
  to CDER PORR XSD validation.

  CONFIRMED CORRECT PATTERN (v29–v32 had no SAX exception):
    subjectOf1/controlActEvent/author[@typeCode="AUT"] with OID .1.7

  C.3.2 ROOT CAUSE:
  ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Machine comparison of v29 vs v30 reporter blocks (confirmed by script):

  Field                  v29 (C.3.2 PASS)       v30 (C.3.2 FAIL)
  ─────────────────────  ─────────────────────  ─────────────────────
  asLocatedEntity        PRESENT                PRESENT  ← NEUTRAL
  org structure          NESTED (2-level)       FLAT (1-level)  ← KEY
  fax: telecom           absent                 present
  <country> in addr      absent                 absent

  FINDING: asLocatedEntity is present in BOTH v29 and v30. It is a
  neutral factor — NOT the C.3.2 differentiator.
  The ONLY confirmed structural difference is nested vs flat org.

  v37 restores the nested org (the sole evidenced fix for C.3.2):
    1. Nested representedOrganization (outer=dept, inner=company)
  v37 also retains asLocatedEntity (neutral, matches v29 baseline)
  v37 adds <country>US</country> to addr (untested in v29/v30; low risk)

  v37 also retains all improvements from v30–v36:
    - <country>US</country> in addr (C.3.4.6)
    - fax: telecom (C.3.4.8)
    - MedDRA indication codes (C.3.4.7 resolved in v30)
    - C.1.7 expedited reporting fields (added in v35)
    - Correct PORR routing (receiver=CDER, wrapper=ZZFDATST)
    - D.7.2 medical history resolved (since v30)
    - No <primaryRole> at investigationEvent level (v33 lesson)

  v37 changes from v36:
    1. New batch UUID (v37)
    2. REMOVED: Two <author> direct children of investigationEvent
    3. ADDED: subjectOf1/controlActEvent/author with OID .1.7 at
       position AFTER outboundRelationship, BEFORE subjectOf2
       (same position as v29 — the only version where C.3.2 passed)
    4. RESTORED: asLocatedEntity in assignedPerson (from v29)
    5. RESTORED: Nested representedOrganization (from v29)
